    {
      "id": "frag-1",
      "focal_uid": 1,
      "title": "The world edges away from the dollar",
      "insight": "The clearest story in the gold models: as countries \u2014 led by the BRICS bloc \u2014 try to trade and hold reserves outside the US dollar, they lean on gold, and that pull runs straight into Chinese buying and the price. Geopolitical friction and inflation both feed the urge to de-dollarize, which is why this sits at the busy centre of the gold map. It's the slow-burn structural bid under the market.",
      "role": "integrator",
